{
  "version": 1,
  "language": "spanish",
  "chapter": 219,
  "title": "También --- Your First Word, Hidden Inside",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:99f1d1991b3e327c",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C58-tambien",
      "sequence": 2330,
      "title": "también — a word with your very first word inside it",
      "headword": "también",
      "romanization": "también",
      "gloss": "also — and you have been holding half of it since the first chapter of this book",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:0321215bd1bc7850",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pero sets two things against each other. Now the opposite move: adding one thing to another."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And say bien, from your first chapter. You will need it in a moment, in a place you would not expect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accent-mark — the accent on también puts the stress on the last syllable: tam-BYEN."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "b-soft — the b here is gentle, the lips barely closing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart: también",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "también = tan + bien."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tan means so, as — it is the word Spanish uses to say how much of something there is. And bien you have had since chapter one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So también is, literally, \"so well\". Somebody says a thing; you say and that goes so well for me too. Say it enough times and it stops being a comment about how well anything is going, and becomes the plain word for also."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Estudio español. Trabajo también."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The most useful shape it takes is the shortest one:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "— Estoy cansado. — Yo también."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words, and you have agreed with somebody. That is worth more in a real conversation than most of the grammar in this book, and it costs nothing to remember, because you already knew half of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice the accent, too. It is there because también is stressed on its last syllable, which is where the bien sits — the borrowed half kept the stress it had when it was a word of its own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Yo también",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Yo también*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Estudio español. Trabajo también.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Estudio español. Trabajo también.*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C58-tambien-agree",
              "prompt": "Somebody says Estoy cansado. Agree, in two words.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-LEX-TAMBIEN"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "yo tambien",
                "yo tambien!"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Two words, and you are in the conversation.",
                "incorrect": "Yo tambien."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C58-tambien-parts",
              "prompt": "What two words is tambien made of?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-ETYMON-TAMBIEN-TAN-BIEN"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 13,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "tan and bien",
                "tan bien, so well"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "So well -- and bien is from your first chapter.",
                "incorrect": "Tan + bien -- so well."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C58-tambien-tan",
              "prompt": "What does tan mean on its own?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-LEX-TAN"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "so",
                "so, as",
                "as"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "It says how much of something there is.",
                "incorrect": "So, or as."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is también, taken apart? (Tan + bien — so well.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And which half have you known since the very beginning? (Bien.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}
